### II. CONTROLLERS - THEORY & INTERVIEW GUIDE

**Theory Explanation:**
Controllers orchestrate the request/response cycle. They contain business logic, validate input, interact with models, and return responses. Single Responsibility Principle: each controller method should do one thing.

**Key Interview Questions:**

**Q: What are controller responsibilities?**
A:
1. Receive request
2. Validate input (via Form Request)
3. Execute business logic
4. Interact with models/services
5. Return response (view, JSON, redirect)

**Q: Explain dependency injection vs direct instantiation**
A:
```php
// BAD - Hard to test, tightly coupled
class PostController {
    public function store(Request $request) {
        $repo = new PostRepository(); // Can't test with mock
        $repo->create($data);
    }
}

// GOOD - Easy to test, loosely coupled
class PostController {
    public function __construct(private PostRepository $repo) {}
    
    public function store(Request $request) {
        $this->repo->create($data);
    }
    
    // Can inject mock in tests
}
```

**Q: When to use service classes?**
A: When business logic gets complex:
```php
// BAD - Logic in controller
public function store(Request $request) {
    $validated = $request->validated();
    
    $user = User::create($validated);
    $user->roles()->attach($request->input('roles'));
    $user->permissions()->attach($request->input('permissions'));
    
    SendWelcomeEmail::dispatch($user);
    CreateActivityLog::dispatch('user.created', $user->id);
    
    return response()->json($user);
}

// GOOD - Logic in service
public function store(Request $request, UserService $service) {
    $user = $service->createWithRolesAndPermissions($request->validated());
    return response()->json($user);
}
```

**Practical Application - Resource Controller Pattern:**

```php
// RESTful API with single responsibility
class PostController extends Controller {
    public function __construct(
        private PostService $service,
        private PostRepository $repo
    ) {}

    public function index(Request $request) {
        // Handle filtering, pagination
        $posts = $this->repo->getPublished()
            ->where('category', $request->category)
            ->paginate();
        
        return PostResource::collection($posts);
    }

    public function store(StorePostRequest $request) {
        $post = $this->service->create($request->validated());
        return new PostResource($post);
    }

    public function show(Post $post) {
        // Increment views (side effect in model)
        $post->incrementViews();
        return new PostResource($post);
    }

    public function update(UpdatePostRequest $request, Post $post) {
        $this->authorize('update', $post);
        $post = $this->service->update($post, $request->validated());
        return new PostResource($post);
    }

    public function destroy(Post $post) {
        $this->authorize('delete', $post);
        $this->service->delete($post);
        return response()->noContent();
    }
}
```

