## IX. TESTING - THEORY & INTERVIEW GUIDE

**Theory Explanation:**
Testing ensures code quality and prevents regressions. Laravel supports feature tests (full request/response) and unit tests (isolated components). Tests improve refactoring confidence and document expected behavior.

**Key Interview Questions:**

**Q: Feature tests vs Unit tests?**
A:
```php
// FEATURE TEST - Full stack test
class PostControllerTest extends TestCase {
    public function test_can_create_post() {
        $response = $this->actingAs(User::factory()->create())
            ->post('/posts', [
                'title' => 'Test Post',
                'body' => 'Test content',
            ]);

        $response->assertRedirect('/posts');
        $this->assertDatabaseHas('posts', ['title' => 'Test Post']);
    }
}

// UNIT TEST - Single component
class PostTest extends TestCase {
    public function test_post_slug_generation() {
        $post = new Post(['title' => 'My First Post']);
        $this->assertEquals('my-first-post', $post->generateSlug());
    }
}
```

**Key Points:**
- Feature tests use real database (test database), slower but comprehensive
- Unit tests mock dependencies, faster, test isolated logic
- Always test happy path and error cases
- Use factories for consistent test data

