## X. CACHING STRATEGY - THEORY & INTERVIEW GUIDE

**Theory Explanation:**
Caching stores expensive operation results to avoid repeating them. Database queries, API calls, and computations are common caching targets. Proper cache invalidation is critical.

**Key Interview Questions:**

**Q: Cache invalidation strategies?**
A:
```php
// 1. Time-based expiration
Cache::put('user.profile.1', $profile, 3600); // 1 hour

// 2. Manual invalidation
Cache::forget('user.profile.1');

// 3. Tag-based invalidation
Cache::tags(['user:1', 'profile'])->put('user.profile.1', $profile);
Cache::tags(['user:1'])->flush(); // Clear all user:1 tagged cache

// 4. Event-based invalidation
class Post extends Model {
    protected static function booted() {
        static::updated(function ($post) {
            Cache::forget("post.{$post->id}");
        });
    }
}
```

**Key Points:**
- Cache drivers: file, database, redis, memcached
- Redis best for production (fastest, supports tags)
- Don't cache everything - only expensive operations
- Set appropriate TTL (time-to-live)

