## XII. DATABASE OPTIMIZATION - THEORY & INTERVIEW GUIDE

**Theory Explanation:**
Database queries are often performance bottlenecks. Optimization involves proper indexing, query design, and access patterns to minimize database load and response times.

**Key Interview Questions:**

**Q: How to identify slow queries?**
A:
```php
// Enable query logging
DB::listen(function ($query) {
    if ($query->time > 1000) { // > 1 second
        Log::warning('Slow query', [
            'sql' => $query->sql,
            'time' => $query->time . 'ms',
            'bindings' => $query->bindings,
        ]);
    }
});

// Use APM tools (DataDog, New Relic, Sentry)
```

**Q: Index strategy?**
A:
```php
// Good indexing
Schema::table('posts', function (Blueprint $table) {
    $table->index('published'); // Single column for WHERE
    $table->index(['user_id', 'published']); // Composite for WHERE user_id = ? AND published
    $table->fullText(['title', 'body']); // Full-text search
});

// Query uses indexes
$posts = Post::where('user_id', 1)
    ->where('published', true)
    ->get();
```

**Key Points:**
- Indexes speed up SELECT/WHERE, slow down INSERT/UPDATE
- B-tree indexes best for range queries
- Full-text indexes best for text search
- Monitor index usage and remove unused ones

