## Core Concepts Explained

### 1. MVC Pattern
```
REQUEST
  ↓
ROUTE → CONTROLLER (Logic) → MODEL (Database)
  ↓                          ↓
  ← ← ← ← ← ← ← ← ← ← ← ← ←
  ↓
 VIEW (HTML)
  ↓
RESPONSE
```

**Model**: Data layer - Eloquent ORM
**View**: Presentation layer - Blade templates
**Controller**: Business logic - Handles requests

---

### 2. Request Lifecycle

```
HTTP Request
    ↓
index.php (Bootstrap)
    ↓
Service Providers (Register services)
    ↓
Middleware (Before)
    ↓
Route Matching
    ↓
Middleware (Route-specific)
    ↓
Controller Action
    ↓
Response Created
    ↓
Middleware (After)
    ↓
HTTP Response
```

---

### 3. Key Terms & Definitions

**Routing**: Mapping URLs to controller actions
```php
Route::get('/posts', [PostController::class, 'index']);
// GET /posts → PostController@index
```

**Middleware**: Request filtering layer
```php
// Executed before reaching controller
// Examples: Authentication, CORS, logging
```

**Eloquent**: Object-Relational Mapping
```php
$user = User::find(1); // Not: $user = DB::select('SELECT * FROM users WHERE id = 1')
```

**Dependency Injection**: Auto-resolving dependencies
```php
public function __construct(PostService $service) {
    // Laravel automatically instantiates PostService
}
```

**Service Container**: Manages application dependencies
```php
app()->bind('service', PostService::class);
app('service')->method();
```

