## Error Handling Patterns

### Pattern 1: Custom Exception Handler
```php
// Custom Exception
class PostNotFoundException extends Exception {
    public function __construct(public int $postId) {
        parent::__construct("Post {$postId} not found");
    }
}

// Exception Handler
class Handler extends ExceptionHandler {
    public function register(): void {
        $this->reportable(function (Throwable $e) {
            // Log with context
            if ($this->shouldReport($e)) {
                Log::error('Exception occurred', [
                    'message' => $e->getMessage(),
                    'user_id' => auth()->id(),
                    'url' => request()->url(),
                    'trace' => $e->getTraceAsString(),
                ]);
            }
        });

        $this->renderable(function (PostNotFoundException $e, Request $request) {
            if ($request->expectsJson()) {
                return response()->json([
                    'message' => 'Post not found',
                    'post_id' => $e->postId,
                ], 404);
            }
            return response()->view('errors.404', [], 404);
        });
    }
}

// Usage
public function show(int $id) {
    $post = Post::find($id);
    
    if (!$post) {
        throw new PostNotFoundException($id);
    }
    
    return view('posts.show', ['post' => $post]);
}
```

**Key Points**:
- Use custom exceptions for clarity
- Log errors with context
- Return appropriate HTTP status codes
- Handle JSON and HTML responses differently

