## Testing Patterns

### Pattern 1: Feature Test
```php
class PostCreationTest extends TestCase {
    // Test happy path
    public function test_authenticated_user_can_create_post() {
        $user = User::factory()->create();
        
        $response = $this->actingAs($user)
            ->post('/posts', [
                'title' => 'My First Post',
                'body' => 'This is the body of my post',
            ]);

        $response->assertRedirect('/posts/1');
        $this->assertDatabaseHas('posts', [
            'title' => 'My First Post',
            'author_id' => $user->id,
        ]);
    }

    // Test validation
    public function test_post_creation_requires_title() {
        $response = $this->actingAs(User::factory()->create())
            ->post('/posts', ['body' => 'No title']);

        $response->assertSessionHasErrors('title');
    }

    // Test authorization
    public function test_user_cannot_delete_others_post() {
        $owner = User::factory()->create();
        $other = User::factory()->create();
        $post = Post::factory()->create(['author_id' => $owner->id]);

        $response = $this->actingAs($other)->delete("/posts/{$post->id}");
        
        $response->assertStatus(403);
        $this->assertDatabaseHas('posts', ['id' => $post->id]); // Not deleted
    }

    // Test unauthenticated access
    public function test_unauthenticated_user_cannot_create_post() {
        $response = $this->post('/posts', ['title' => 'Test']);
        
        $response->assertRedirect('/login');
    }
}
```

**Key Points**:
- Test happy path and error cases
- Test authorization
- Test validation
- Use factories for test data
